  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For three low density gases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> pressure versus temperature graphs are plotted while keeping them at constant volume, as shown in the figure</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0053_da28e849656d.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 179px;\" /></p><p>The temperature corresponding to the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>373</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
